# CS Demo Manager CLI on the game VM (the demo analyzer). Read by ci-demo-analysis-setup.sh, which
# installs this version through analyzer-maintenance.sh, and by install-analyzer.sh.
#
# Bump it when a CS2 update breaks demo parsing (as the 11 November 2026 update did for 3.20.1):
#   1. version and the .deb's sha256 from the release (gh release view vX -R akiver/cs-demo-manager
#      --json assets, the "digest" field);
#   2. CSDM_SCHEMA = CURRENT_SCHEMA_VERSION in src/node/database/migrations/migrate-database.ts;
#   3. if the schema changes, port the new migration to backend/migrations/ (see csdm_schema_15.sql)
#      and update the table list in backend/migrations/csdm_analyzer_role.sql.
# The setup workflow installs the CLI only once the production schema equals CSDM_SCHEMA, because the
# CLI refuses any other version and its restricted database role cannot migrate.
CSDM_VERSION=3.21.0
CSDM_DEB_SHA256=12b43418d0a0e7d2e714d7ad04505697933043c5e456f81ea934c96d74b6ce65
CSDM_SCHEMA=15
